Claim 02 — Telegram goal creation
=================================

Goal: locate the /new_goal handler entry point in src/telegram/ with >=2
path:line citations and decide whether a live Telegram demo can run in
this goal worker session.

Method: static inspection only (Grep + Read). No live Telegram message
was sent.

Code evidence
-------------

1. Command registration (handler entry)
   src/telegram/goal-commands.ts:1959-1960

       // /new_goal <text> (with /goal as backward-compatible alias)
       bot.command(["new_goal", "goal"], async (ctx: TelegramGoalCommandContext) => {

   The Telegram bot binds both `/new_goal` and the legacy `/goal` alias
   to the same async handler. The handler resolves auth, captures the
   reply-to message id, and either calls handleGoal("", cfg) for the
   empty-text help reply or schedules runGoalInBackground -> handleGoal
   to plan the goal.

2. Command spec / bot menu
   src/telegram/goal-commands.ts:97-99

       export const GOAL_COMMAND_SPECS: Array<{ command: string; description: string }> = [
         { command: "new_goal", description: "Plan a new goal (shows plan for approval)" },

   /new_goal is the first entry in the published Telegram command set,
   so it is the documented public entrypoint.

3. Empty-input fallback / usage string
   src/telegram/goal-commands.ts:484-487

       export async function handleGoal(text: string, config?: MoltbotConfig): Promise<GoalPlanResult> {
         if (!text.trim()) {
           return { text: "Usage: /new_goal <description of what you want to achieve>" };
         }

   Confirms the user-visible /new_goal prompt shape.

