Live-test posture
-----------------

A live Telegram demo would require a running Moltbot gateway, an
authenticated Telegram bot token, and a real chat. None of that can be
exercised inside this goal worker:

  * The gateway service must not be restarted during goal execution
    (hard deny on systemctl --user restart and moltbot gateway restart).
  * Sending real Telegram messages from this worker would create
    user-visible side effects and is explicitly out of scope (the goal
    brief says "Do not send Telegram messages to a live bot").
  * No Telegram bot credentials are present in the worker environment.

Therefore the runtime portion of this claim is marked manual-required.
The code path itself is verified: the `/new_goal` command is wired,
documented, tested, and reachable.

Safe README wording (drawn from code, not aspirational)
-------------------------------------------------------

  * "Start a goal from Telegram with /new_goal <description>; the bot
    replies with the plan for approval before any work runs."
  * "The same goal pipeline is also reachable from the CLI."

Unsafe wording to avoid
-----------------------

  * "Fully automated Telegram approval" — buttons, reactions and
    /goal_approve are all manual operator actions.
  * "Verified end-to-end via Telegram in this audit" — this audit did
    not send a live Telegram message; only the handler is verified.

STATUS: partial
